      "content": "1.2 Geographical Location"
    },
    {
      "id": "u3rb2cq",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "ehq6fi6",
      "src": "/books/Guide/RAJASTHAN SI GS GUIDE/images/image_ehq6fi6.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Rajasthan is situated between 23°3' North to 30°12' North latitude and 69°30' East to 78°17' East longitude.",
      "id": "bwc8z58"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "It shares its boundaries with the following states and a neighbouring country:",
      "id": "jhcll7y"
    },
    {
      "id": "t04w204",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "North: Punjab and Haryana",
        "North-East: Uttar Pradesh",
        "East: Madhya Pradesh",
        "South-East: Madhya Pradesh",
        "South: Gujarat",
        "West: Pakistan (International Border – Radcliffe Line)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The total length of the international border with Pakistan (Radcliffe Line) is approximately 1,070 km, passing through the districts of Ganganagar, Bikaner, Jaisalmer, and Barmer.",
      "id": "z3htmu6"
    },
    {
      "id": "q47kfy3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1.3 Districts and Divisions"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Rajasthan has 50 districts (after the 2023 reorganisation). Earlier, it had 33 districts. The 10 new districts created in 2023 are: Anupgarh, Balotra, Beawar, Deeg, Dudu, Gangapur City, Jaipur Rural, Jodhpur Rural, Kekri, Kotputli-Behror, Neem Ka Thana, Phalodi, Salumbar, Sanchore, Shahpura (Bhilwara), Shahpura (Jaipur).",
      "id": "q1boiat"
    },
